## Clues
1-3. A letter in the Greek alphabet. ~ GAMMA
4-2. A trap. ~ SNARE
7-5. Part of a mandolin. ~ FRETS
6-8. Situations. ~ SITES
9-10. A scheme. ~ PLAN
11-12. Earth containing carbonate of lime, etc. ~ MARL
13-14. It falls from the sky. ~ RAIN
15-16. Land parched with heat. ~ ARID
17-18. Fermented malt liquor. ~ ALE
19-20. A gentle blow. ~ PAT
21-22. To point. ~ AIM
23-24. A title used in addressing a man. ~ SIR
25-26. A province in Austria. ~ MORAVIA
27-28. To levy. ~ ESTREAT
25-27. Honey of roses. ~ MELROSE
26-28. To affect injuriously. ~ ATTAINT
29-30. Made with eggs. ~ OMELETS
31-32. Inactivity. ~ INERTIA
33-34. Distinguished. ~ EMINENT
35-36. A crystalline compound contained in animal and vegetable fats. ~ STEARIN
17-3. Words and music. ~ ARIA
18-4. They come before Christmas. ~ EVES
19-3. A supplication. ~ PLEA
20-5. You have ten. ~ TOES
4-23. Complete assortments. ~ SETS
6-24. A commotion. ~ STIR
5-21. A bristle. ~ SETA


